# Web Component Development Ruleset for Electric Maybe Shopify Theme

## 🎯 Project Overview
This is a Shopify theme project for Electric Maybe agency. All web components should follow professional standards with modern JavaScript practices, performance optimizations, and accessibility considerations.

## 🏗️ Core Principles

### 1. **Professional Architecture**
- Use ES6+ class syntax with proper inheritance
- Implement complete lifecycle management
- Follow single responsibility principle
- Maintain clean separation of concerns

### 2. **Performance First**
- Use passive event listeners where possible
- Implement proper cleanup in disconnectedCallback
- Avoid memory leaks with proper event listener management
- Optimize for garbage collection
- Target performance: Component initialization < 16ms, Event processing < 8ms

### 3. **Accessibility & Standards**
- Follow WCAG 2.1 AA guidelines
- Use semantic HTML and ARIA attributes
- Ensure keyboard navigation support
- Maintain proper focus management

## 📋 Required Structure for All Web Components

### Class Definition
```javascript
/**
 * ComponentName - Brief description
 * Detailed description of functionality and purpose
 * 
 * @example
 * <component-name data-attribute="value">
 *   Content here
 * </component-name>
 */
class ComponentName extends HTMLElement {
  // Private fields MUST be declared at class level with # syntax
  #isConnected = false;
  #config = {};
  #state = {};

  constructor() {
    super();
    
    // Bind methods to preserve context
    this.handleEvent = this.handleEvent.bind(this);
    
    // Initialize private properties
    this.#initializeState();
  }
}
```

### Lifecycle Methods
```javascript
/**
 * Lifecycle method called when element is connected to DOM
 */
connectedCallback() {
  if (this.#isConnected) return;
  
  try {
    this.#attachEventListeners();
    this.#initializeComponent();
    this.#isConnected = true;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('ComponentName: Failed to initialize', error);
  }
}

/**
 * Lifecycle method called when element is disconnected from DOM
 */
disconnectedCallback() {
  if (!this.#isConnected) return;
  
  try {
    this.#removeEventListeners();
    this.#cleanup();
    this.#isConnected = false;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('ComponentName: Failed to cleanup', error);
  }
}
```

## 🔒 Privacy & Encapsulation

### Private Fields (Use `#` syntax - REQUIRED)
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - True privacy (MANDATORY)
#isConnected = false;
#config = {};
#state = {};

// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Convention only
_isConnected = false;
_config = {};
```

### Private Methods (Use `#` syntax - REQUIRED)
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - True privacy (MANDATORY)
#initializeComponent() { /* ... */ }
#attachEventListeners() { /* ... */ }
#cleanup() { /* ... */ }

// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Convention only
_initializeComponent() { /* ... */ }
```

## 📡 Component Communication (Pub/Sub Pattern)

### **Use Custom Events for Component Communication**
Instead of direct method calls between components, use the pub/sub pattern with custom events:

```javascript
// ✅ Publisher Component (dispatching events)
class PromoBanner extends HTMLElement {
  #handleClose() {
    try {
      // Dispatch custom event for other components to listen to
      this.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('promo-banner:closed', {
        detail: { 
          bannerHeight: this.offsetHeight,
          timestamp: Date.now()
        },
        bubbles: true
      }));
      this.remove();
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('PromoBanner: Error closing banner:', error);
    }
  }
}

// ✅ Subscriber Component (listening for events)
class HeaderElement extends HTMLElement {
  connectedCallback() {
    // Listen for events from other components
    document.addEventListener('promo-banner:closed', this.handlePromoBannerClosed.bind(this));
  }

  disconnectedCallback() {
    // Always clean up event listeners
    document.removeEventListener('promo-banner:closed', this.handlePromoBannerClosed.bind(this));
  }

  handlePromoBannerClosed(event) {
    // Handle the event and update component state
    this.updateOffsets();
  }
}
```

### **Benefits of Pub/Sub Pattern**
- **Decoupled**: Components don't need to know about each other's implementation
- **Flexible**: Easy to add/remove subscribers without changing publishers
- **Maintainable**: Method names can change without breaking communication
- **Extensible**: Multiple components can listen to the same events
- **Testable**: Events can be easily mocked and tested

### **Event Naming Convention**
- Use descriptive names: `component:action` (e.g., `promo-banner:closed`, `cart:item-added`)
- Include relevant data in `event.detail`
- Set `bubbles: true` for cross-component communication
- Use `composed: true` if you need to cross shadow DOM boundaries

### **When to Use Pub/Sub**
- ✅ **Component-to-component communication**
- ✅ **Cross-component state updates**
- ✅ **User action notifications**
- ✅ **Lifecycle event broadcasting**

### **When NOT to Use Pub/Sub**
- ❌ **Internal component state management**
- ❌ **Direct parent-child communication (use props/attributes)**
- ❌ **Simple data passing (use method parameters)**

## 📝 Documentation Standards

### JSDoc Comments (REQUIRED)
```javascript
/**
 * Brief description of the method
 * @param {Type} paramName - Description of parameter
 * @param {Object} options - Configuration options
 * @param {string} options.key - Description of option
 * @returns {Type} Description of return value
 * @throws {Error} Description of when error is thrown
 * @private
 */
#methodName(paramName, options = {}) {
  // Implementation
}
```

### Class Documentation (REQUIRED)
```javascript
/**
 * ComponentName - Brief description
 * 
 * Detailed description including:
 * - Purpose and functionality
 * - Usage examples
 * - Dependencies
 * - Browser support requirements
 * 
 * @example
 * <component-name data-attribute="value">
 *   Content here
 * </component-name>
 */
```

## 🎛️ Event Handling

### Event Listener Configuration
```javascript
#eventOptions = {
  passive: true,    // For scroll/touch events
  capture: false,   // Default to bubbling
  once: false       // Default to persistent
};

#attachEventListeners() {
  this.addEventListener('click', this.handleClick, this.#eventOptions);
  this.addEventListener('keydown', this.handleKeydown, this.#eventOptions);
}
```

### Event Handler Methods
```javascript
/**
 * Handle click events
 * @param {MouseEvent} event - The click event
 */
handleClick(event) {
  this.#processEvent(event, 'click');
}

/**
 * Handle keyboard events
 * @param {KeyboardEvent} event - The keyboard event
 */
handleKeydown(event) {
  if (event.key === 'Enter' || event.key === ' ') {
    this.#processEvent(event, 'keydown');
  }
}
```

## 🛡️ Error Handling

### Try-Catch Patterns (REQUIRED)
```javascript
#processEvent(event, eventType) {
  try {
    // Event processing logic
    this.#validateEvent(event);
    this.#dispatchCustomEvent(eventType, data);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`ComponentName: Error processing ${eventType}`, error);
    this.#handleError(error);
  }
}

#handleError(error) {
  // Graceful error handling
  // Dispatch error event for parent components
  this.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('component-error', {
    detail: { error, component: this.tagName },
    bubbles: true
  }));
}
```

## 🔧 Static Methods & Utilities

### Validation Methods
```javascript
/**
 * Validate component configuration
 * @param {Object} config - Configuration object
 * @returns {boolean} - Whether configuration is valid
 */
static isValidConfig(config) {
  return config && typeof config === 'object';
}

/**
 * Get all instances of this component
 * @returns {NodeList} - Collection of component instances
 */
static getAllInstances() {
  return document.querySelectorAll(this.tagName.toLowerCase());
}
```

### Utility Methods
```javascript
/**
 * Debounce function calls
 * @param {Function} func - Function to debounce
 * @param {number} wait - Wait time in milliseconds
 * @returns {Function} - Debounced function
 */
static debounce(func, wait) {
  let timeout;
  return function executedFunction(...args) {
    const later = () => {
      clearTimeout(timeout);
      func(...args);
    };
    clearTimeout(timeout);
    timeout = setTimeout(later, wait);
  };
}
```

## 🧪 Testing Considerations

### Testable Structure
```javascript
// Expose methods for testing (only in development)
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {
  ComponentName.prototype._testOnly = {
    getState: () => this.#state,
    getConfig: () => this.#config,
    triggerEvent: (eventType) => this.#processEvent({}, eventType)
  };
}
```

### Event Testing
```javascript
// Dispatch events that can be tested
#dispatchCustomEvent(eventType, detail) {
  const event = new CustomEvent(eventType, {
    detail,
    bubbles: true,
    cancelable: true
  });
  
  this.dispatchEvent(event);
  return event; // Return for testing
}
```

## 📦 Registration & Export

### Custom Element Registration
```javascript
// Register the custom element with safety check
if (!customElements.get('component-name')) {
  customElements.define('component-name', ComponentName);
}
```

### Module Export
```javascript
// Export for module usage
if (typeof module !== 'undefined' && module.exports) {
  module.exports = ComponentName;
}

// Export for ES modules
if (typeof exports !== 'undefined') {
  exports.ComponentName = ComponentName;
}
```

## 🎨 CSS & Styling

### Shadow DOM Usage
```javascript
constructor() {
  super();
  
  // Use shadow DOM for encapsulation
  this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' });
  this.#render();
}

#render() {
  this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `
    <style>
      :host {
        display: block;
        /* Component styles */
      }
    </style>
    <div class="component">
      <!-- Component template -->
    </div>
  `;
}
```

## 🔄 State Management

### State Updates
```javascript
#updateState(newState) {
  const oldState = { ...this.#state };
  this.#state = { ...this.#state, ...newState };
  
  // Trigger re-render if needed
  if (this.#shouldRerender(oldState, this.#state)) {
    this.#render();
  }
  
  // Dispatch state change event
  this.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('state-change', {
    detail: { oldState, newState: this.#state },
    bubbles: true
  }));
}
```

## 📊 Performance Monitoring

### Performance Hooks
```javascript
#measurePerformance(operation, callback) {
  const start = performance.now();
  const result = callback();
  const duration = performance.now() - start;
  
  // Log slow operations
  if (duration > 16) { // Longer than one frame
    console.warn(`ComponentName: Slow ${operation} took ${duration.toFixed(2)}ms`);
  }
  
  return result;
}
```

## 🚀 Usage Examples

### Basic Implementation
```javascript
/**
 * ExampleComponent - Demonstrates component usage
 * Handles user interactions and dispatches events
 */
class ExampleComponent extends HTMLElement {
  #isConnected = false;
  #state = { count: 0 };
  #eventOptions = { passive: true, capture: false };

  constructor() {
    super();
    this.handleClick = this.handleClick.bind(this);
  }

  connectedCallback() {
    if (this.#isConnected) return;
    
    try {
      this.#attachEventListeners();
      this.#render();
      this.#isConnected = true;
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('ExampleComponent: Failed to initialize', error);
    }
  }

  disconnectedCallback() {
    if (!this.#isConnected) return;
    
    try {
      this.#removeEventListeners();
      this.#isConnected = false;
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('ExampleComponent: Failed to cleanup', error);
    }
  }

  #attachEventListeners() {
    this.addEventListener('click', this.handleClick, this.#eventOptions);
  }

  #removeEventListeners() {
    this.removeEventListener('click', this.handleClick, this.#eventOptions);
  }

  handleClick(event) {
    this.#processEvent(event, 'click');
  }

  #processEvent(event, eventType) {
    try {
      this.#updateState({ count: this.#state.count + 1 });
      this.#dispatchCustomEvent(eventType, { count: this.#state.count });
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(`ExampleComponent: Error processing ${eventType}`, error);
    }
  }

  #updateState(newState) {
    this.#state = { ...this.#state, ...newState };
    this.#render();
  }

  #render() {
    this.innerHTML = `<button>Count: ${this.#state.count}</button>`;
  }

  #dispatchCustomEvent(eventType, detail) {
    const event = new CustomEvent(eventType, {
      detail,
      bubbles: true,
      cancelable: true
    });
    this.dispatchEvent(event);
  }

  static getCount() {
    return document.querySelectorAll('example-component').length;
  }
}

if (!customElements.get('example-component')) {
  customElements.define('example-component', ExampleComponent);
}
```

## 🎯 File-Specific Rules

### For `_scripts/*.js` files:
- Must follow web component patterns from ruleset
- Use true private fields/methods with `#` syntax
- Include proper lifecycle management
- Implement error handling and logging
- Add comprehensive JSDoc documentation
- Include static utility methods
- Use performance optimizations

### For `sections/*.liquid` files:
- Follow Shopify Liquid best practices
- Use semantic HTML structure
- Include proper ARIA attributes
- Optimize for performance and accessibility

### For `snippets/*.liquid` files:
- Maintain reusability and modularity
- Use consistent naming conventions
- Include proper documentation comments
- Follow DRY principles

## 🌐 Browser Support
Target modern browsers (Chrome 74+, Firefox 90+, Safari 15+) for private class fields and methods. Use fallbacks for older browsers when necessary.

## 📈 Performance Targets
- Component initialization: < 16ms
- Event processing: < 8ms
- Memory usage: No leaks, proper cleanup
- Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance

